==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Witchy Neneko''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Costumed Witchy Neneko''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Gloomy Neneko is nearly exactly the same as normal [[Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Neneko]]. Now, she has lower damage in exchange for a higher critical chance. She might be slightly better or worse in places you would use her normal variant, but still, her niche usage is practically nonexistent due to the existence of cats with a lower cooldown or better stats, like [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]]. She doesn't have [[Sister Act (Combo)|Sister Act]] like her original form either, so she's not going to last once you enter mid-game scenarios. As with all Neneko variants, general usage is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
At first glance, her true form seems promising since Wave-blockers are incredibly rare and valuable. Unfortunately, Gloomy Neneko's True Form has a series of problems that hinder her overall performance. Firstly, her survivability is questionable as she only has 15k hp and 3 knockbacks. And considering her long cooldown, a Gloomy Neneko can perish quickly and leave you with no protection against Waves. Leveling her with [[Catseye]]s can help alleviate that problem, but it's important to note that it's a big investment. Neneko does however have an ace up her spooky sleeve: range. All of the current non-Uber Wave-blockers rely on either tanking hits or sniping Waves, instead of standing far enough to completely avoid Wave-generating attacks. Neneko can also be used in tandem with [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] as extra defense for essentially free.

Overall, Costumed Witchy Neneko's niche of a ranged Wave Blocker is that she doesn't get outranged like Octopus Cat, and she has a short enough cooldown to compete with other ranged wave blockers, only losing out in terms of durability. As such, clever use of this unit is necessary, but when done properly, it can trivialize wave stages with terrifying ease.

